  "title": "CHAPTER 4: MAHARASHTRA POLITY AND GOVERNANCE",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "sb0az01",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Maharashtra Legislature (Vidhan Sabha and Vidhan Parishad)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Maharashtra operates with a bicameral legislature consisting of the Vidhan Sabha (Legislative Assembly) and Vidhan Parishad (Legislative Council).",
        "Executive administration at the state level is headed by the Governor and Chief Minister.",
        "Local self-governance in Maharashtra is divided into Urban Local Bodies and Rural Local Bodies (Panchayati Raj).",
        "State law enforcement encompasses a structured Maharashtra Police force, Commissionerates, and Special Police Forces.",
        "The Maharashtra Public Service Commission (MPSC) conducts major recruitment tests, including the Sub-Inspector of Police (Non-Technical) Exam."
      ],
      "id": "wzdon5n"
    },
